      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "df= pd.read_csv(\"./data/processed/penguins_cleaned.csv\")\n",
        "df.head()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import random\n",
        "np.random.seed(42)\n",
        "random.seed(42)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "hIofwHG9JpWD"
      },
      "execution_count": 4,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 3,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0BqO8NgAyunO"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Select significant features\n",
        "features = ['bill_length_mm', 'bill_depth_mm', 'flipper_length_mm', 'body_mass_g']\n",
        "X = df[features]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Standardize feature for clustering\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
        "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
        "X_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0BqO8NgAyunO"
      },
      "execution_count": 2,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "IOP625aKTHk6"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Feature Selection\n",
        "\n",
        "We selected the following features for clustering and dimensionality reduction:\n",
        "\n",
        "- bill_length  \n",
        "- bill_depth  \n",
        "- flipper_length  \n",
        "- body_mass  \n",
        "\n",
        "These features represent key physical characteristics of penguins, capturing both size (body mass, flipper length) and morphology (bill dimensions). They are continuous and exhibit meaningful variation across species, making them suitable for distance-based algorithms such as K-Means.\n",
        "\n",
        "Additionally, these features are biologically interpretable and allow us to distinguish between species based on measurable physical traits."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 4,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "wdlPClYBzk6f"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Train Clustering (K-Means)\n",
        "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
        "\n",
        "kmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=3, random_state=42)\n",
        "labels = kmeans.fit_predict(X_scaled)\n",
        "df['cluster'] = labels"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "wdlPClYBzk6f"
      },
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 5,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "hPKsrYkIzt_L",
        "outputId": "b9baaecb-f958-4ca3-b75f-b1ed53defedf"
      },
      "execution_count": 4,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "0.44428701706572565\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Evaluation\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import silhouette_score\n",
        "sil_score = silhouette_score(X_scaled, labels)\n",
        "print(sil_score)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 6,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "ppMOm0cDz7dG",
        "outputId": "d6c0f2e1-9f25-4101-c978-d95cc328328e"
      },
      "execution_count": 5,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "0.7802764801745099\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.metrics import adjusted_rand_score\n",
        "ari = adjusted_rand_score(df['species'], labels)\n",
        "print(ari)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qICvBu4nWV33"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Model Evaluation\n",
        "\n",
        "We evaluate clustering performance using two metrics:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Silhouette Score: measures how well-separated the clusters are\n",
        "- Adjusted Rand Index (ARI): compares clustering results with true species labels\n",
        "\n",
        "Results:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Silhouette Score: 0.44428701706572565\n",
        "- ARI Score: 0.7802764801745099\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "The Silhouette Score indicates a moderate level of separation between clusters. This suggests that while clusters are reasonably well-formed, there is still some overlap between them.\n",
        "\n",
        "On the other hand, the ARI score is relatively high, indicating that the clustering aligns well with the true species labels.\n",
        "\n",
        "This combination reveals an important insight: although the model successfully captures the underlying structure of the data, the boundaries between clusters are not perfectly distinct. In particular, some species share similar physical characteristics, leading to overlapping regions in feature space.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "26vRbn9n0Lh-"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Dimensionality reduction\n",
        "from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n",
        "\n",
        "pca = PCA(n_components=2)\n",
        "X_pca = pca.fit_transform(X_scaled)\n",
        "\n",
        "df['PC1'] = X_pca[:, 0]\n",
        "df['PC2'] = X_pca[:, 1]"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "26vRbn9n0Lh-"
      },
      "execution_count": 6,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 13,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Save dataset\n",
        "df.to_csv(\"./data/processed/penguins_pca.csv\")"
      ]
    },
